1
00:00:02,302 --> 00:00:03,827
ED: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:04,037 --> 00:00:08,099
I hope you know, Oswald,
you can always count on me.

3
00:00:11,578 --> 00:00:12,807
COBBLEPOT: Thank you.

4
00:00:14,581 --> 00:00:17,244
Miss Kringle, dinner.

5
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:18,551
<i>Chez moi.</i>

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,520
Okay.

7
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:21,687
(GRUNTS)

8
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:24,447
That was for Kristen.

9
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:26,426
VALE: <i>Whatever
happened with Tetch?</i>

10
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:28,525
Broke his sister out of GCPD.

11
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:29,729
I'll never go with you!

12
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,090
- I love you!
- You're insane!

13
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:32,359
No, no!

14
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:33,623
- No!
- (THUDDING)

15
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,800
(CRYING)

16
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:36,735
<i>You killed her!</i>

17
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:38,263
JIM: <i>She died. He escaped.</i>

18
00:00:38,472 --> 00:00:41,465
'Cause I heard a rumor there's
something strange about her blood.

19
00:00:49,583 --> 00:00:51,108
I'll tell you what
you wanna know.

20
00:00:52,085 --> 00:00:54,350
You are gonna have to buy
me dinner, though. (SIGHS)

21
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:55,984
He killed you.

22
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:57,550
(GAGGING)

23
00:00:58,258 --> 00:01:02,753
Those who hurt
you will feel my pain.

24
00:01:05,032 --> 00:01:08,059
(ALL CHEERING)

25
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:15,771
- I love you, Daddy.
- I love you, too, baby.

26
00:01:16,043 --> 00:01:17,636
- So proud of you.
- (CHUCKLING)

27
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:22,540
Bye!

28
00:01:32,993 --> 00:01:34,757
(BOTH LAUGHING)

29
00:01:35,195 --> 00:01:37,315
- Well, the good part is about to happen.
- I hope so.

30
00:01:37,864 --> 00:01:40,959
Look at that, there's no
greater symbol of love

31
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:46,065
than two people who've made the choice
to spend the rest of their lives together.

32
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:50,835
Hey, pal, we have a reception to get
to. So, what you say we get a move on?

33
00:01:51,011 --> 00:01:54,243
Oh, yes. About that. I'm afraid
you won't be able to attend.

34
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:57,945
This some kind of a joke?

35
00:01:58,719 --> 00:01:59,743
No.

36
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:02,915
It's quite serious, in fact.

37
00:02:03,757 --> 00:02:05,658
- (BRIDE CHUCKLES)
- You're needed elsewhere.

38
00:02:07,194 --> 00:02:08,958
- Let's get out of here.
- Yeah.

39
00:02:09,363 --> 00:02:12,424
- Hey, open the damn door!
- Sorry, we mustn't be late.

40
00:02:12,666 --> 00:02:14,328
Please, just don't hurt us.

41
00:02:14,835 --> 00:02:17,134
That's not my decision to make.

42
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:20,733
Your fate depends
entirely on James Gordon.

43
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:22,699
Hey! Hey!

44
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,808
Don't forget to buckle up.

45
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,581
GROOM: <i>Help! Help!</i> BRIDE: <i>Help!</i>

46
00:02:28,749 --> 00:02:30,741
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

47
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:37,822
What a beautiful morning.

48
00:02:39,026 --> 00:02:41,461
Sun is shining,
birds are singing.

49
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:42,923
(SIGHS)

50
00:02:43,597 --> 00:02:46,294
They say that fortune
favors the brave.

51
00:02:48,402 --> 00:02:50,530
Do they have that saying
in your country, Olga?

52
00:02:50,704 --> 00:02:52,070
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

53
00:02:52,406 --> 00:02:54,466
(SCOFFS) I don't
know what you're saying.

54
00:02:54,641 --> 00:02:56,269
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

55
00:02:56,977 --> 00:03:01,938
It's not important. What is important
is that I have found someone.

56
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:06,710
What good is love
if it's one-sided?

57
00:03:07,154 --> 00:03:08,154
(SNIFFS)

58
00:03:08,655 --> 00:03:11,454
I have no choice but to
confess my feelings to Ed.

59
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:13,456
<i>- Da.</i>
- (CHUCKLES)

60
00:03:13,727 --> 00:03:16,720
Now that, I understand.
It means yes.

61
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:18,992
My mother taught me that.

62
00:03:19,332 --> 00:03:23,827
She used to tell me, "Life only
gives you one true love, Oswald.

63
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:27,305
"When you find it, run to it."

64
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,401
So, that is what
I'm going to do.

65
00:03:32,579 --> 00:03:35,105
I'm also going to enroll
you in an ESL program.

66
00:03:35,348 --> 00:03:37,828
You really should learn the
language if you're gonna work here.

67
00:03:43,423 --> 00:03:46,791
So, I hear that Lee Thompkins is
running point on Alice Tetch's blood

68
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,858
- at the GCPD.
- (SIGHS)

69
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:50,758
That would make sense.

70
00:03:51,331 --> 00:03:52,731
Can you get me a
sit-down with her?

71
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:54,194
(CHUCKLES)

72
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:58,133
Oh, I see. You're willing to help
me, just not when it comes to your ex.

73
00:03:58,371 --> 00:03:59,371
It's complicated.

74
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:01,166
Actually, it's really simple.

75
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:03,853
You just pick up the phone, you
dial her number and you let her know

76
00:04:03,877 --> 00:04:07,211
that Valerie Vale would like a
sit-down to discuss Alice Tetch's blood.

77
00:04:07,447 --> 00:04:09,348
See? It's pretty simple.

78
00:04:11,985 --> 00:04:13,180
She won't give you anything.

79
00:04:13,453 --> 00:04:14,493
You leave that part to me.

80
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:18,115
You know, I can
get used to this,

81
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:20,350
you helping me with my stories.

82
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,322
- We make a pretty good team.
- Mmm.

83
00:04:22,796 --> 00:04:24,273
Does that mean you'll
share your breakfast?

84
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:27,927
Absolutely not. But really, when
are you gonna give up this Pl act?

85
00:04:28,602 --> 00:04:32,095
<i>So far, you've had two cases.
One girl died and the other one...</i>

86
00:04:32,405 --> 00:04:33,464
<i>Well, you never found her.</i>

87
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:35,231
In baseball, we
call that an O-fer.

88
00:04:36,476 --> 00:04:38,308
- I'm happy.
<i>- Of course you are.</i>

89
00:04:38,512 --> 00:04:40,592
You get to drink scotch all
day and have sex with me.

90
00:04:41,181 --> 00:04:42,205
Ah...

91
00:04:42,549 --> 00:04:44,279
I gotta go to work.

92
00:04:45,318 --> 00:04:46,513
You know what?

93
00:04:47,154 --> 00:04:48,315
This is nice.

94
00:04:50,557 --> 00:04:52,197
Let me know when you
hear from Thompkins.

95
00:04:54,728 --> 00:04:56,356
JIM: Uh-huh.

96
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:06,663
Can I help you?

97
00:05:06,907 --> 00:05:10,002
James Gordon, Jervis
Tetch has a message for you.

98
00:05:12,345 --> 00:05:16,339
"Follow my friend where to go to
learn the truth you've hidden below.

99
00:05:16,716 --> 00:05:20,710
<i>"Should you choose not to play,
precious people will die today."</i>

100
00:05:34,067 --> 00:05:36,161
(PHONE RINGING)

101
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,981
- This is Gordon.
- Hello, James.

102
00:05:48,748 --> 00:05:51,946
Jervis, never should've left
that hole you were hiding in.

103
00:05:52,252 --> 00:05:56,280
Oh, I wasn't just hiding. I
put the time to good use.

104
00:05:57,257 --> 00:06:00,785
Made a thorough study of
you. Quite the fascinating history.

105
00:06:00,994 --> 00:06:03,987
Yet, so tragic. A father, lost.

106
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:07,656
<i>Career gone by the
wayside. Failed relationships.</i>

107
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:10,400
And here I didn't
think about you once.

108
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:12,163
(CHUCKLING) Oh, James.

109
00:06:13,306 --> 00:06:14,986
I've been inside that
head of yours, James.

110
00:06:15,775 --> 00:06:19,109
I've seen the web of
lies you tell yourself.

111
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:23,874
Strung together to keep that
fragile psyche of yours intact.

112
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:25,728
Well, it's been nice
catching up with you.

113
00:06:25,752 --> 00:06:28,950
<i>I'm going to force you to
confront who you really are.</i>

114
00:06:29,289 --> 00:06:32,623
And I'm going to
drive you mad doing it.

115
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:35,428
<i>Now, please, direct
your eyes to the overpass.</i>

116
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:38,494
<i>Meet Dave and Amy Walters.</i>

117
00:06:39,366 --> 00:06:42,803
Married just this
morning. Lovely ceremony.

118
00:06:43,103 --> 00:06:45,299
In 30 seconds, they're
going to jump to their deaths.

119
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,132
<i>Take the stairs, and
you can save them.</i>

120
00:06:47,307 --> 00:06:49,708
However, down the
street, there's a little boy.

121
00:06:50,210 --> 00:06:52,907
<i>His name is Shane. And
he's going to be hit by a truck</i>

122
00:06:53,146 --> 00:06:55,809
<i>driven by my highly
esteemed associate.</i>

123
00:06:56,549 --> 00:06:57,676
(TIRES SCREECHING)

124
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:02,715
<i>Choice is yours, James.</i>

125
00:07:05,558 --> 00:07:07,390
You can't save both.

126
00:07:09,329 --> 00:07:11,321
So, who's it going to be?

127
00:07:36,690 --> 00:07:38,352
(THUDDING)

128
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,111
- JERVIS: <i>You can't save both of them.</i>
- (PHONE RINGING)

129
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:51,127
<i>You can't save both of them.</i>

130
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:03,148
You son of a bitch.

131
00:08:03,416 --> 00:08:05,016
JERVIS: <i>Good. Now
I have your attention.</i>

132
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:07,363
They were innocent, Jervis.
You didn't have to kill them.

133
00:08:07,387 --> 00:08:11,552
<i>It was your choice, James. You
practically pushed them off the ledge.</i>

134
00:08:12,025 --> 00:08:14,256
<i>Stay with me, James. James?</i>

135
00:08:14,561 --> 00:08:15,561
What?

136
00:08:15,895 --> 00:08:18,421
<i>87 Fulton Street. Apartment
Four-C. Five minutes.</i>

137
00:08:18,698 --> 00:08:21,566
<i>No police, or more people die.</i>

138
00:08:24,738 --> 00:08:26,934
(SIRENS WAILING)

139
00:08:29,209 --> 00:08:31,906
Oh, boy. Now it's official?

140
00:08:32,212 --> 00:08:33,372
Why? You looking to back out?

141
00:08:33,813 --> 00:08:35,338
You'd have to
put a bullet in me.

142
00:08:35,582 --> 00:08:36,822
Good thing I don't carry a gun.

143
00:08:37,217 --> 00:08:38,217
(CHUCKLES)

144
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:43,420
My father called. (CLEARS THROAT)
He wants to throw us an engagement party.

145
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:45,682
- Told him we're not interested.
- Okay.

146
00:08:46,126 --> 00:08:48,152
I know you had reservations
about moving back here.

147
00:08:48,461 --> 00:08:50,501
And you know my dad. Half
measures aren't his thing.

148
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:53,462
If we say yes, he's gonna put
us on display for the whole city.

149
00:08:53,733 --> 00:08:54,826
I understand.

150
00:08:56,469 --> 00:08:58,199
But we chose to
build a life here.

151
00:08:58,471 --> 00:08:59,471
And I'm glad.

152
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,839
An engagement party
sounds wonderful.

153
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:05,576
(INHALES SHARPLY)

154
00:09:06,746 --> 00:09:09,682
These go directly to
the City Clerk's office.

155
00:09:11,117 --> 00:09:13,450
And, this...

156
00:09:17,123 --> 00:09:19,854
Leave this outside Nicky
The Nail's place. Knock twice.

157
00:09:20,026 --> 00:09:21,927
Light it and then run.

158
00:09:22,195 --> 00:09:23,595
WOMAN: Okay.

159
00:09:27,867 --> 00:09:29,067
Good morning, Mayor Cobblepot.

160
00:09:29,369 --> 00:09:31,167
Good morning to
you, my Chief of Staff.

161
00:09:31,438 --> 00:09:32,715
Here are your
schedules for the day.

162
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:35,766
This covers your duties as Mayor
and this as kingpin of the underworld.

163
00:09:36,042 --> 00:09:39,308
(CHUCKLES) You really are settling
into your role here, aren't you, Ed?

164
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,980
And yet, I still have so
much to learn from you.

165
00:09:44,317 --> 00:09:46,013
(BOTH CLEAR THROATS)

166
00:09:48,121 --> 00:09:50,056
I came up empty
tracking down Butch.

167
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,954
Somehow, that one-handed
ape managed to disappear.

168
00:09:54,194 --> 00:09:56,959
I suspect he's hiding
with his old crew.

169
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:00,238
I'm sorry for letting you down.

170
00:10:01,534 --> 00:10:03,969
You have done
nothing of the sort.

171
00:10:04,404 --> 00:10:06,600
I would be lost without you.

172
00:10:09,309 --> 00:10:10,538
In fact, um,

173
00:10:11,144 --> 00:10:13,340
there is something
that I need to tell you.

174
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,306
Something very important.

175
00:10:23,723 --> 00:10:25,453
What is it, Oswald?

176
00:10:30,063 --> 00:10:32,225
You know what? I
forget. (LAUGHS)

177
00:10:33,399 --> 00:10:36,494
In and out of my head just like that.
Don't you hate that, when that happens?

178
00:10:36,769 --> 00:10:37,769
That never happens to me.

179
00:10:38,104 --> 00:10:42,166
You know what? I believe that.
So, where are we off to first?

180
00:10:42,442 --> 00:10:44,638
PS 134. You're touring a school.

181
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:48,013
Press will be there, so
we better get a move on.

182
00:10:48,248 --> 00:10:51,343
(CHUCKLES)
Great. I love children.

183
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:52,710
(CLEARS THROAT)

184
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:57,188
Okay, thank you very much. Good.

185
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,555
Hey, Cap! I just spoke
to that kid over there.

186
00:11:03,796 --> 00:11:06,960
You're not gonna believe this.
He said Jim Gordon saved his life.

187
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,680
Pulled him out of
the way of a truck.

188
00:11:08,868 --> 00:11:10,029
Get him on the phone. Now.

189
00:11:10,303 --> 00:11:12,499
I already tried him. No answer.

190
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:17,940
What happened?
You forget your cane?

191
00:11:18,444 --> 00:11:19,810
I don't need it anymore.

192
00:11:20,647 --> 00:11:23,811
Put an all-points out on
Gordon. I want him found.

193
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:29,880
Hey, does that guy look strange to you?
I mean, more so than the usual wackjob?

194
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:32,024
Hey, pal!

195
00:11:32,792 --> 00:11:33,987
You see what happened here?

196
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,421
Have a message for you.

197
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:38,529
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

198
00:11:39,599 --> 00:11:41,568
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

199
00:11:41,935 --> 00:11:42,935
He's hypnotized.

200
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:44,647
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

201
00:11:44,671 --> 00:11:45,969
Tetch.

202
00:12:22,875 --> 00:12:24,867
(PHONE RINGING)

203
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,425
Jervis.

204
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:41,992
JERVIS: <i>Cutting it close, James.</i>

205
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:43,505
I like what you've
done with the place.

206
00:12:43,529 --> 00:12:45,361
<i>Everyone needs a hobby.</i>

207
00:12:46,165 --> 00:12:47,428
<i>Take a peek through the lens.</i>

208
00:12:47,734 --> 00:12:49,669
<i>Let's chat face-to-face.</i>

209
00:12:53,573 --> 00:12:56,941
<i>I wonder, what is it that you
have against married couples?</i>

210
00:12:57,644 --> 00:12:59,442
<i>Bad memories, perhaps?</i>

211
00:12:59,746 --> 00:13:00,907
<i>Understandable.</i>

212
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:04,116
<i>Given the last time you saw
a woman in a wedding dress,</i>

213
00:13:04,417 --> 00:13:06,215
<i>she had a shotgun
pointed at you.</i>

214
00:13:06,552 --> 00:13:07,552
Hey, Jervis.

215
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:08,846
<i>Yes, James?</i>

216
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:12,819
(PHONE RINGING)

217
00:13:17,363 --> 00:13:18,363
Hello?

218
00:13:18,665 --> 00:13:20,896
<i>- Don't you ever do that again!</i>
- Okay.

219
00:13:23,202 --> 00:13:24,295
(PHONE RINGING)

220
00:13:24,570 --> 00:13:26,163
This is about
your sister, isn't it?

221
00:13:26,406 --> 00:13:28,766
In your addled brain, you blame
me for what happened to her.

222
00:13:28,941 --> 00:13:29,941
<i>Don't you talk about her!</i>

223
00:13:30,176 --> 00:13:32,236
I got to know her, Jervis.
She was a good person.

224
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,969
That's why she hated you.

225
00:13:34,213 --> 00:13:37,012
Why she died trying
to get away from you.

226
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:39,481
You want revenge? Kill yourself.

227
00:13:39,719 --> 00:13:42,188
<i>Dismissive. Rude. I
don't like your attitude.</i>

228
00:13:42,522 --> 00:13:45,492
I'll tell you what. I'll come down.
We can talk about it in person.

229
00:13:45,758 --> 00:13:47,420
<i>Hang up again, she dies.</i>

230
00:13:49,062 --> 00:13:50,302
What're you talking about? Who?

231
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,026
<i>Surprising, really.</i>

232
00:13:52,298 --> 00:13:56,360
Given that every relationship
you've been in ended in such misery.

233
00:13:56,969 --> 00:14:00,030
And yet, you made
the choice to date again.

234
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:04,702
Poor girl, she had no idea who
she was getting into bed with.

235
00:14:06,079 --> 00:14:08,344
She will soon. See for yourself.

236
00:14:11,384 --> 00:14:13,285
<i>Great thing about reporters.</i>

237
00:14:14,787 --> 00:14:18,383
Tell them you have a story,
and they'll meet you anywhere.

238
00:14:21,227 --> 00:14:22,559
(MUFFLED) Let me go!

239
00:14:36,342 --> 00:14:38,402
I've got him in a
safe house uptown.

240
00:14:38,644 --> 00:14:40,844
You would not believe the
amount of steak that man eats.

241
00:14:40,913 --> 00:14:43,644
Poor, Butchie. Nothing but
Tabitha and red meat all day.

242
00:14:44,317 --> 00:14:47,515
You know, sooner or later, Penguin
is gonna figure out who sprung him.

243
00:14:47,854 --> 00:14:49,914
- You need a plan, sweetie.
- I'm working on it.

244
00:14:50,189 --> 00:14:52,954
And in the meantime? Has the
flame rekindled between you two?

245
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:54,717
Or are you still holding out?

246
00:14:55,194 --> 00:14:56,234
- We'll see.
- (DOOR OPENS)

247
00:14:56,796 --> 00:14:58,389
Oh, speaking of old flames...

248
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,629
Well, you just can't
seem to stay away.

249
00:15:01,868 --> 00:15:03,029
Tetch. Where is he?

250
00:15:03,302 --> 00:15:07,433
How should I know? And if you don't
mind, Tabitha and I are just in the...

251
00:15:08,307 --> 00:15:09,307
Unnecessary.

252
00:15:09,542 --> 00:15:11,320
Jervis Tetch kidnapped
Valerie Vale this morning.

253
00:15:11,344 --> 00:15:13,024
He knew things only
you could've told him.

254
00:15:13,279 --> 00:15:14,799
- I want to know where he is.
- (SIGHS)

255
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:17,509
See that fire? I mean, where
was that when we were together?

256
00:15:17,817 --> 00:15:19,285
All I got was Captain Vanilla.

257
00:15:21,187 --> 00:15:22,187
(BARBARA SIGHS)

258
00:15:22,889 --> 00:15:25,791
Seriously, we have
to open in a few hours.

259
00:15:26,058 --> 00:15:27,058
Then talk.

260
00:15:27,293 --> 00:15:29,524
Firstly, I don't know
where Tetch is.

261
00:15:29,862 --> 00:15:32,764
Secondly, he may have come in
here a few days ago asking about you.

262
00:15:33,032 --> 00:15:34,032
Asking what?

263
00:15:34,233 --> 00:15:36,259
Oh, you know, everything.

264
00:15:36,836 --> 00:15:38,737
Family stuff, GCPD.

265
00:15:39,038 --> 00:15:41,803
The women in your life. He
seemed especially interested in that.

266
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:45,408
He knew all about Vale
already, but I told him about us.

267
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:49,337
About how you're still in love with
me. Cry yourself to sleep at night.

268
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:52,449
And Lee? Did you
tell him about her?

269
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:56,146
Oh, you mean Miss
Rebound from me? Of course.

270
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:59,117
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

271
00:15:59,392 --> 00:16:02,157
We'll send you a
bill for the damage!

272
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:03,657
Lee, listen to me.

273
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:06,308
JERVIS: <i>I'm sorry, James. Lee
can't come to the phone right now.</i>

274
00:16:06,332 --> 00:16:07,527
<i>Can I take a message?</i>

275
00:16:07,834 --> 00:16:09,200
No? Good.

276
00:16:09,602 --> 00:16:11,400
Gotham Water and
Power, 10 minutes.

277
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:14,129
I need to know if she's
okay. Both Lee and Vale.

278
00:16:14,373 --> 00:16:17,434
<i>What you want means
nothing to me. Nine minutes.</i>

279
00:16:21,681 --> 00:16:23,445
James sends his regards.

280
00:16:23,749 --> 00:16:25,775
Now, where were we?

281
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:31,985
Oh, yes. Introductions. Lee
Thompkins meet Valerie Vale.

282
00:16:32,258 --> 00:16:35,422
You both have one very
important thing in common.

283
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:39,594
You're two halves
of Jim Gordon's heart.

284
00:16:47,106 --> 00:16:49,507
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

285
00:16:49,775 --> 00:16:51,767
Where is Jervis Tetch?

286
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:54,704
- James Gordon, I have a message for you.
- (SIGHS)

287
00:16:54,981 --> 00:16:57,951
Yeah, I know. You said that
the first 100 times I asked you.

288
00:16:58,317 --> 00:17:00,286
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

289
00:17:00,586 --> 00:17:03,112
Where is he? I know
you can hear me!

290
00:17:03,289 --> 00:17:04,882
(METAL CREAKING)

291
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,494
(GRUNTING)

292
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:15,930
Hey, Cap! A Uni just spotted Gordon
pulling up to Gotham Water and Power.

293
00:17:16,335 --> 00:17:19,305
Tell him to hold his
position till we get there.

294
00:17:52,605 --> 00:17:54,801
<i>Glad you could make it, James.</i>

295
00:17:57,043 --> 00:17:58,170
Where's Lee and Vale?

296
00:17:58,444 --> 00:18:00,538
<i>Oh, you clearly have
no sense for stagecraft.</i>

297
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:02,874
<i>We must build to the climax.</i>

298
00:18:03,115 --> 00:18:07,644
<i>This is merely the second
act, where we stoke the tension.</i>

299
00:18:10,323 --> 00:18:14,988
<i>On the right is one of
Gotham's finest pediatricians.</i>

300
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:18,592
<i>On the left, Channel
Five's favorite anchor.</i>

301
00:18:18,798 --> 00:18:21,927
<i>A doctor and a
journalist. You get it?</i>

302
00:18:22,201 --> 00:18:23,201
Yeah, I get it.

303
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:26,895
<i>The choice is simple, you see.
It's kill one and the other will go free.</i>

304
00:18:27,139 --> 00:18:31,372
<i>But if your answer to me is
no, 1,000 watts into them will go.</i>

305
00:18:48,561 --> 00:18:50,530
Sorry, Jervis, I'm
not killing anyone.

306
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:53,823
<i>Yes, you will. Now pick
up the pistol and fire!</i>

307
00:18:54,266 --> 00:18:56,997
You want to show me who
I really am? Then show me.

308
00:18:57,503 --> 00:18:58,527
<i>Oh, I will.</i>

309
00:18:58,838 --> 00:18:59,918
I'm done playing your game.

310
00:19:00,272 --> 00:19:01,296
BULLOCK: <i>Jim!</i>

311
00:19:04,744 --> 00:19:07,009
Hold! What the hell
is going on here?

312
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:12,582
<i>Captain Barnes, you're just in time to
see James kill these two innocent men.</i>

313
00:19:12,952 --> 00:19:14,672
We need to find the
main power shutoff. Now.

314
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:15,820
Go!

315
00:19:16,055 --> 00:19:19,219
<i>Even when you don't choose,
James, there are consequences.</i>

316
00:19:20,693 --> 00:19:23,094
(MUFFLED SCREAMING)

317
00:19:23,963 --> 00:19:25,158
JIM: <i>No!</i>

318
00:19:32,405 --> 00:19:34,431
No. No!

319
00:19:37,376 --> 00:19:38,376
I'm gonna find you.

320
00:19:38,611 --> 00:19:42,207
<i>Oh, I'm counting on it. Just ask
an old friend how to get to the end.</i>

321
00:19:48,054 --> 00:19:49,488
(SCHOOL BELL RINGING)

322
00:19:49,789 --> 00:19:51,951
This is our third grade class.

323
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,784
(KIDS CHATTERING)

324
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,804
How many more grades
do we have to visit?

325
00:19:55,828 --> 00:19:57,421
This is a K through 12 building.

326
00:19:57,763 --> 00:19:59,095
- Twelve?
- Mmm-hmm.

327
00:19:59,165 --> 00:20:01,259
But, we don't have to see
every single class, do we?

328
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:03,297
Mayor James used
to read to the children.

329
00:20:03,636 --> 00:20:05,195
Aubrey James is
illiterate, ma'am.

330
00:20:05,504 --> 00:20:08,030
- It's well documented.
- Perhaps we should move on.

331
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:09,140
(GASPS)

332
00:20:10,576 --> 00:20:11,896
What's wrong
with that boy there?

333
00:20:14,547 --> 00:20:15,640
That's Luke.

334
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:18,275
He's new here.

335
00:20:29,428 --> 00:20:32,057
Hello, Luke. I am
Mayor Cobblepot.

336
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:34,605
Why aren't you playing
with the other children?

337
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,998
What if they don't like me?

338
00:20:37,503 --> 00:20:41,099
Well, how would you ever
know if you don't give it a try?

339
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,434
And if they don't like you,

340
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:48,305
wait for them to turn their backs
and push them down the stairs.

341
00:20:53,152 --> 00:20:54,586
(CHUCKLES)

342
00:20:57,289 --> 00:20:58,769
Little guy needed
a push, that's all.

343
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:02,225
I continue to be in
awe of you, Oswald.

344
00:21:07,333 --> 00:21:08,357
Ed...

345
00:21:10,035 --> 00:21:14,166
There is something I would like
to discuss in a more private setting.

346
00:21:15,775 --> 00:21:18,267
Shall we say dinner
at the mansion? 8:00?

347
00:21:18,978 --> 00:21:20,498
I'll pick us up a
nice bottle of wine.

348
00:21:21,347 --> 00:21:22,371
(CHUCKLES)

349
00:21:24,416 --> 00:21:26,851
Tetch has Lee Thompkins
and Valerie Vale. You're sure?

350
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:30,385
I saw him take Vale and I
called Lee's cell and he answered.

351
00:21:30,656 --> 00:21:31,783
So, yeah, pretty sure.

352
00:21:32,057 --> 00:21:35,118
Call the ME's office.
Call her fiancé. Find her!

353
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:39,629
What the hell is going on here?

354
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:43,329
Tetch blames me for
what happened to his sister.

355
00:21:43,602 --> 00:21:44,626
He wants revenge.

356
00:21:44,870 --> 00:21:47,430
So what? He kills two innocent
civilians? How does that track?

357
00:21:47,706 --> 00:21:50,175
He's obsessed with
showing me who I really am.

358
00:21:50,409 --> 00:21:52,139
Driving me insane.

359
00:21:52,945 --> 00:21:55,437
He killed them, and
I just stood there!

360
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:58,117
What were you supposed
to do? Shoot one of them?

361
00:21:58,384 --> 00:22:00,250
You did what you
could. That's on him.

362
00:22:00,753 --> 00:22:02,847
This is just to prepare me.

363
00:22:07,359 --> 00:22:08,399
He's gonna make me choose.

364
00:22:09,695 --> 00:22:11,994
He's gonna put me in
front of Lee and Vale,

365
00:22:12,231 --> 00:22:14,860
and he's gonna make
me choose. And if I don't...

366
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:16,432
He'll kill both of them.

367
00:22:20,506 --> 00:22:21,530
We're gonna find her.

368
00:22:22,541 --> 00:22:24,271
I promise you that.

369
00:22:25,477 --> 00:22:29,642
Listen to me. Tetch is a
lunatic. He's gonna get caught.

370
00:22:29,882 --> 00:22:32,442
The most you can hope for is a
lifetime in prison. Don't do this.

371
00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:35,951
Dumfree, let's see
what's in the kitchen.

372
00:22:37,523 --> 00:22:38,855
Mmm-hmm.

373
00:22:43,329 --> 00:22:44,592
Nice try.

374
00:22:45,431 --> 00:22:46,942
So, why'd they bring
us back to your place?

375
00:22:46,966 --> 00:22:47,966
Like I know?

376
00:22:48,167 --> 00:22:49,477
<i>Any chance your boyfriend
might come home?</i>

377
00:22:49,501 --> 00:22:50,525
Not likely.

378
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:52,203
(SIGHS)

379
00:22:53,806 --> 00:22:55,417
You do know what
this is about, don't you?

380
00:22:55,441 --> 00:22:58,673
Yes. Tetch blames Jim for his sister,
and we're his means for revenge.

381
00:22:58,911 --> 00:22:59,911
<i>I've been here before.</i>

382
00:23:00,112 --> 00:23:02,946
That's too big. It's never
going to spring the mechanism.

383
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:06,761
You know, it is kind
of ironic, though.

384
00:23:06,785 --> 00:23:10,517
I was just asking Jim to get me a
sit-down with you. And here we are.

385
00:23:10,589 --> 00:23:11,589
Uh-huh.

386
00:23:12,791 --> 00:23:15,420
See, I'm writing a story
on Alice Tetch's blood.

387
00:23:15,694 --> 00:23:18,493
I know you're running
point for the GCPD.

388
00:23:19,932 --> 00:23:22,277
You're not seriously trying to
interview me right now, are you?

389
00:23:22,301 --> 00:23:25,465
- Jim said you wouldn't talk to me.
- And he was right.

390
00:23:25,971 --> 00:23:28,873
I think he was just
being protective of you.

391
00:23:30,676 --> 00:23:31,735
Anyway, about Alice Tetch.

392
00:23:32,011 --> 00:23:35,243
I hear they're running experiments
on her blood at the GCPD bio facility.

393
00:23:35,514 --> 00:23:36,514
Care to comment?

394
00:23:36,749 --> 00:23:39,189
Maybe you're just really scared
and this is your way of coping

395
00:23:39,218 --> 00:23:41,258
or maybe you're just
insanely committed to your job.

396
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,915
Either way, all I'm interested
in is getting out of here.

397
00:23:45,391 --> 00:23:49,226
Try a cuticle pusher. My dad was
a cop. Taught me how to pick locks.

398
00:23:49,561 --> 00:23:50,722
I can walk you through it.

399
00:23:51,697 --> 00:23:52,697
Thank you.

400
00:23:53,165 --> 00:23:55,285
And in exchange, you can
talk to me about Alice Tetch.

401
00:23:56,235 --> 00:23:57,675
You and Jim are
made for each other.

402
00:23:58,437 --> 00:23:59,530
Thanks.

403
00:23:59,805 --> 00:24:01,137
It's not a compliment.

404
00:24:01,473 --> 00:24:04,875
Thank you, Dr. Calvi. I'll call
you as soon as we hear anything.

405
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:07,136
Mario's been in
surgery all morning.

406
00:24:07,479 --> 00:24:11,007
Says that he and Lee left the
house together this morning.

407
00:24:11,317 --> 00:24:13,757
She was headed to the station.
He hasn't heard from her since.

408
00:24:13,986 --> 00:24:15,830
Jervis must have grabbed
her before she got here.

409
00:24:15,854 --> 00:24:17,516
What's his next move?

410
00:24:17,823 --> 00:24:18,903
Tetch wants me to find him.

411
00:24:19,158 --> 00:24:21,803
Well, if that's the case, then why
didn't he just tell you where he is?

412
00:24:21,827 --> 00:24:23,427
I don't know. But
the last thing he said

413
00:24:23,529 --> 00:24:25,657
was something about an
old friend leading me to him.

414
00:24:26,498 --> 00:24:30,629
Well, I'm not just gonna sit here and
wait for Tetch to send you an invitation.

415
00:24:31,971 --> 00:24:33,303
Listen up!

416
00:24:33,839 --> 00:24:38,209
Jervis Tetch thinks that Gotham
is his personal playground.

417
00:24:38,877 --> 00:24:40,675
He's taken innocent lives.

418
00:24:40,946 --> 00:24:43,541
And now, he has Lee
Thompkins and Valerie Vale.

419
00:24:44,049 --> 00:24:46,678
<i>And to whoever puts
the collar on Tetch,</i>

420
00:24:46,986 --> 00:24:50,115
<i>my personal gratitude
and best bottle of brown.</i>

421
00:24:50,422 --> 00:24:51,549
<i>Now, go to work.</i>

422
00:24:51,857 --> 00:24:54,053
MAN: <i>Follow my
friend where to go.</i>

423
00:24:55,761 --> 00:24:58,424
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

424
00:24:58,697 --> 00:25:01,189
James Gordon, I have
a message for you.

425
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,400
Hey!

426
00:25:03,035 --> 00:25:04,503
James Gordon?

427
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,772
I have a message for you.

428
00:25:10,009 --> 00:25:11,807
How do I get to the end?

429
00:25:33,966 --> 00:25:38,199
"The true test will be revealed.
A final decision you must yield.

430
00:25:39,438 --> 00:25:41,600
"Tea party begins once more,

431
00:25:44,443 --> 00:25:47,311
"when you walk through
Lee Thompkins' door."

432
00:25:56,822 --> 00:25:58,484
- Jim.
- Not now.

433
00:25:58,791 --> 00:26:00,783
What the hell's going
on? Where's Lee?

434
00:26:06,198 --> 00:26:07,838
Look, you're just
gonna have to trust me.

435
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,798
Trust you? According
to Captain Barnes,

436
00:26:10,035 --> 00:26:11,713
you're the reason she's
in trouble to begin with.

437
00:26:11,737 --> 00:26:14,104
You know something. You
know where she is, don't you?

438
00:26:14,373 --> 00:26:16,399
(GRUNTS) Keep your voice down.

439
00:26:16,675 --> 00:26:18,007
Does Barnes know? Where is he?

440
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:20,735
No. He does not know. Because,
if he showed up with 20 cops,

441
00:26:21,013 --> 00:26:22,675
both Lee and Vale would be dead.

442
00:26:23,015 --> 00:26:27,214
I see. So, you're going to go in
all alone and save them? Is that it?

443
00:26:28,220 --> 00:26:32,157
Actually, you might be the only
person who can help me. Come on.

444
00:26:34,626 --> 00:26:37,061
- Remember, you have to feel...
- I got it.

445
00:26:39,164 --> 00:26:40,462
Can I ask you something?

446
00:26:40,766 --> 00:26:42,598
As long as it's not
about Alice Tetch's blood.

447
00:26:45,404 --> 00:26:47,396
Why'd you move back to Gotham?

448
00:26:47,639 --> 00:26:50,939
The way I hear it, you made a
pretty nice life for yourself down South.

449
00:26:51,276 --> 00:26:54,110
- It's really none of your business.
- Maybe not.

450
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:56,642
But you could've moved to
any city. Gotten a new job.

451
00:26:56,982 --> 00:26:59,008
Yet, you chose
Gotham and the GCPD.

452
00:26:59,318 --> 00:27:01,378
You realize that we both
might die today, right?

453
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:04,389
Mmm-hmm. Well?

454
00:27:06,859 --> 00:27:11,194
I didn't come here for James Gordon,
if that's what you're worried about.

455
00:27:12,698 --> 00:27:13,893
- Not bad.
- (SIGHS)

456
00:27:14,266 --> 00:27:15,757
- My turn.
- Okay.

457
00:27:16,034 --> 00:27:18,046
- Okay, so what's our plan?
- You're gonna break free.

458
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:21,110
We're gonna lure in one of these goons.
Hit him over the head with something.

459
00:27:21,740 --> 00:27:24,835
Not good. Um, you
can still get out of here.

460
00:27:25,110 --> 00:27:27,830
I'm not leaving you here. There's
gotta be something else we can use.

461
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:29,212
JERVIS: <i>My, my.</i>

462
00:27:30,682 --> 00:27:32,412
You two have been busy.

463
00:27:32,684 --> 00:27:35,848
Now, if you'd kindly join
me in the dining room.

464
00:27:36,255 --> 00:27:38,554
The guest of honor
will be here shortly.

465
00:27:52,271 --> 00:27:54,536
(OPERA MUSIC PLAYING)

466
00:28:06,418 --> 00:28:08,478
Welcome to our tea party, James.

467
00:28:08,787 --> 00:28:10,779
<i>We've been expecting you.</i>

468
00:28:19,264 --> 00:28:20,562
Please...

469
00:28:25,003 --> 00:28:26,403
Have a seat.

470
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:33,171
- I think I'll stand.
- You'll do what I say.

471
00:28:33,445 --> 00:28:34,845
Or things will get messy.

472
00:28:35,147 --> 00:28:38,413
And by messy, I mean, my
two friends will pull their triggers.

473
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:43,155
And then we'll have blood and
brains all over this beautiful table. So...

474
00:28:45,490 --> 00:28:48,756
Place your gun on the
platter and have a seat.

475
00:28:51,129 --> 00:28:52,153
<i>Really?</i>

476
00:28:52,431 --> 00:28:55,458
After all we've been through
today, you have to think about it?

477
00:28:55,767 --> 00:28:57,895
<i>Not everyone here has to die.</i>

478
00:29:17,389 --> 00:29:19,017
It's going to be okay.

479
00:29:19,858 --> 00:29:21,190
Don't lie to them, James.

480
00:29:22,394 --> 00:29:26,263
Lee, would you mind
passing that down to James?

481
00:29:27,466 --> 00:29:30,698
I must apologize
for the hideous china.

482
00:29:30,969 --> 00:29:34,428
(CHUCKLES) Frankly, I expected
more from Don Falcone's son.

483
00:29:35,674 --> 00:29:37,674
Guess I know what I'm
getting you for your wedding.

484
00:29:38,310 --> 00:29:39,403
(JERVIS SIGHS)

485
00:29:41,847 --> 00:29:43,372
To good health.

486
00:29:43,882 --> 00:29:45,851
- I think I'll pass.
- Me, too.

487
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:49,181
You know what?

488
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:51,616
I'll have some.

489
00:29:54,059 --> 00:29:55,459
<i>Bravo, James.</i>

490
00:29:59,364 --> 00:30:04,598
Now, I'd like to begin by telling
the story of a brother and a sister,

491
00:30:04,936 --> 00:30:08,532
<i>separated for years, but
whose love never waned.</i>

492
00:30:09,308 --> 00:30:10,640
Fair warning though,

493
00:30:12,110 --> 00:30:13,840
it has a sad ending.

494
00:30:33,532 --> 00:30:36,195
But, I couldn't find
my sister alone.

495
00:30:36,468 --> 00:30:39,370
<i>So I turned to this
man, James Gordon.</i>

496
00:30:39,638 --> 00:30:42,972
Whom everyone said was a
good man, an honorable man.

497
00:30:43,308 --> 00:30:46,972
And what did this good man
do? Why, he found my sister

498
00:30:47,245 --> 00:30:48,679
and he turned her against me!

499
00:30:48,947 --> 00:30:51,781
Poisoning her mind!
And then he killed her!

500
00:30:55,220 --> 00:30:56,711
Does that sound
about right, James?

501
00:30:56,988 --> 00:30:59,082
- Sure. Why not?
- Now, James.

502
00:30:59,891 --> 00:31:01,826
I get the sense you're
not being honest.

503
00:31:02,094 --> 00:31:03,619
<i>Though, that's not surprising</i>

504
00:31:03,895 --> 00:31:08,196
<i>considering you've run from
your true self every day of your life.</i>

505
00:31:08,467 --> 00:31:10,402
<i>But you can't run
from this choice.</i>

506
00:31:10,936 --> 00:31:12,928
The woman you love

507
00:31:13,605 --> 00:31:15,267
is going to die.

508
00:31:17,175 --> 00:31:19,610
<i>I just need to figure
out which one it is.</i>

509
00:31:20,078 --> 00:31:24,174
So, let's review our
options, shall we?

510
00:31:36,361 --> 00:31:40,321
On the one hand, we
have Lee Thompkins.

511
00:31:40,966 --> 00:31:43,197
Intelligent. Kind.

512
00:31:43,468 --> 00:31:45,869
She thought she could
save you from your darkness.

513
00:31:46,138 --> 00:31:50,098
Drag you into the light. And what
did she get for her efforts, hmm?

514
00:31:52,344 --> 00:31:55,542
- Pain and sadness.
- Don't listen to him, Lee.

515
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:03,020
Look in her eyes,

516
00:32:06,258 --> 00:32:08,693
she still has love
for you, James.

517
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:13,025
And then there's Valerie Vale.

518
00:32:13,698 --> 00:32:17,226
The intrepid reporter
from a blue-collar family.

519
00:32:18,203 --> 00:32:20,297
She still has hope for you.

520
00:32:22,007 --> 00:32:25,500
What will happen when she
learns who you really are?

521
00:32:26,344 --> 00:32:27,344
<i>So,</i>

522
00:32:28,313 --> 00:32:31,044
those are the choices.

523
00:32:33,452 --> 00:32:34,977
Now, it's up to you.

524
00:32:35,253 --> 00:32:38,348
Which lady

525
00:32:39,291 --> 00:32:40,486
has your heart?

526
00:32:40,692 --> 00:32:42,126
Who do you love?

527
00:32:43,929 --> 00:32:46,990
You want me to choose? Tell
these idiots to lower their guns.

528
00:32:47,232 --> 00:32:49,072
I don't trust them not
to shoot me by accident.

529
00:32:49,301 --> 00:32:51,497
You're right. They are
stupid. (CHUCKLES)

530
00:32:52,037 --> 00:32:53,437
Down, boys.

531
00:32:54,339 --> 00:32:55,830
Now, you drop your gun.

532
00:32:56,141 --> 00:32:59,077
- And why would I do that?
- Because I'll shoot you.

533
00:33:03,248 --> 00:33:05,808
- Well, well.
- You okay?

534
00:33:06,785 --> 00:33:08,378
<i>This was your grand plan, James?</i>

535
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:13,320
Play along until Dr. Calvi could
sneak in and shoot me dead?

536
00:33:14,226 --> 00:33:15,785
<i>But, there's only
one small problem.</i>

537
00:33:16,695 --> 00:33:18,664
Before you arrived, I
went down to the basement

538
00:33:18,897 --> 00:33:21,128
and switched the magazine
in that gun with an empty one.

539
00:33:21,466 --> 00:33:22,593
(GUN CLICKS)

540
00:33:22,901 --> 00:33:24,836
My apologies, Dr. Calvi.

541
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:27,062
I only set the table for four.

542
00:33:27,305 --> 00:33:30,969
Dumfree, will you please
escort the doctor to the bathroom.

543
00:33:31,543 --> 00:33:34,274
I believe there's still one
chain in working order.

544
00:33:36,982 --> 00:33:40,111
Now, I'm out of patience!

545
00:33:41,887 --> 00:33:44,379
Who do you love?

546
00:33:44,656 --> 00:33:48,354
You want to talk about love?
Fine. Let's talk about who you love.

547
00:33:48,627 --> 00:33:50,027
- Or, loved.
<i>- Don't.</i>

548
00:33:50,295 --> 00:33:52,423
- Your sister knew you were crazy, Jervis.
- Stop it.

549
00:33:52,664 --> 00:33:55,998
- She was terrified of you. She hated you.
- Enough.

550
00:33:56,234 --> 00:33:57,532
She told me,

551
00:33:58,236 --> 00:34:00,637
what you did to her
when you were kids.

552
00:34:01,907 --> 00:34:04,376
- The thought of you disgusted her.
- Lies! Deceit!

553
00:34:04,609 --> 00:34:07,443
The story you tell is
incomplete! She loved me!

554
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:10,876
She loved you? She killed
herself rather than be with you.

555
00:34:11,116 --> 00:34:12,140
She didn't! No.

556
00:34:12,417 --> 00:34:15,410
She impaled herself on
a spike and died in agony.

557
00:34:15,687 --> 00:34:18,521
Because, even that was
better than having you touch her.

558
00:34:18,823 --> 00:34:21,156
- No, no, no, no, no, no.
<i>- I saw her.</i>

559
00:34:21,459 --> 00:34:23,860
<i>When she was dying. Her face...</i>

560
00:34:24,596 --> 00:34:27,589
When she knew she
was finally safe from you,

561
00:34:27,999 --> 00:34:31,993
she was smiling. Because,
despite the pain, she was happy.

562
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:33,705
Liar!

563
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:37,471
She was the only
thing I ever loved,

564
00:34:37,709 --> 00:34:41,669
and you, you sent her
soul to heaven above.

565
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:43,905
Yes. That's right.

566
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:47,409
Me. I'm the one you want.

567
00:34:47,852 --> 00:34:51,584
So, let Lee and
Vale go. Keep me.

568
00:34:51,957 --> 00:34:54,051
But let them go.

569
00:34:58,997 --> 00:35:01,330
Oh, James.

570
00:35:01,866 --> 00:35:03,061
(SIGHS)

571
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:06,169
You're trying to confuse me.

572
00:35:08,707 --> 00:35:11,006
But I won't let you. No.

573
00:35:11,309 --> 00:35:14,609
I'm determined
that you'll live on,

574
00:35:14,980 --> 00:35:18,417
and suffer without
your love as I have.

575
00:35:20,018 --> 00:35:21,018
Choose.

576
00:35:25,223 --> 00:35:28,625
- No. I won't choose.
- You will! You will!

577
00:35:29,027 --> 00:35:30,757
You'll certainly spill.

578
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:38,231
(INHALES DEEPLY)

579
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:40,366
I'll make it easy for you.

580
00:35:40,772 --> 00:35:44,436
On the count of three, instead
of telling me who you love,

581
00:35:46,011 --> 00:35:48,207
tell me who to kill.

582
00:35:50,348 --> 00:35:54,376
Or I shoot both of them,
which would be such a thrill.

583
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:56,622
(HEART POUNDING)

584
00:35:57,489 --> 00:35:58,513
One.

585
00:36:04,796 --> 00:36:05,957
Two.

586
00:36:12,804 --> 00:36:14,602
- Three.
- Kill Lee.

587
00:36:14,773 --> 00:36:15,773
(GASPS)

588
00:36:16,474 --> 00:36:18,067
Oh, finally.

589
00:36:18,410 --> 00:36:23,041
The truth is revealed. You
chose Lee because you love Vale.

590
00:36:24,015 --> 00:36:25,210
Very well.

591
00:36:25,450 --> 00:36:26,975
(GRUNTS)

592
00:36:27,285 --> 00:36:29,151
I knew you had it in you, James.

593
00:36:29,387 --> 00:36:34,325
All this time, you made everyone
believe you were the hero.

594
00:36:34,559 --> 00:36:36,994
But deep down, you
always knew the truth.

595
00:36:37,762 --> 00:36:39,390
You're a villain.

596
00:36:43,234 --> 00:36:44,327
Vale.

597
00:36:47,238 --> 00:36:48,763
<i>This is Dr. Leslie Thompkins.</i>

598
00:36:48,973 --> 00:36:52,205
Please send an ambulance
to 25 Blackstone Drive. Hurry!

599
00:36:52,610 --> 00:36:53,610
Move.

600
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:58,043
You're going to be okay, Vale.
You hear me, you're going to be okay.

601
00:36:58,283 --> 00:36:59,546
Hold on.

602
00:37:05,690 --> 00:37:07,318
Victim's name is Valerie Vale.

603
00:37:07,625 --> 00:37:09,423
Gunshot wound to the abdomen.

604
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:12,755
BP is 100 over
60. Tachy's at 160.

605
00:37:13,131 --> 00:37:15,123
OR One's prepped
and ready to go.

606
00:37:15,467 --> 00:37:17,902
Clear the way! Clear
the way, please.

607
00:37:18,636 --> 00:37:19,636
I got it from here.

608
00:37:37,322 --> 00:37:40,019
("LA VIE EN ROSE"
PLAYING ON STEREO)

609
00:37:41,025 --> 00:37:42,425
Ed.

610
00:37:43,027 --> 00:37:47,260
A man comes to a crossroads in
his life, and he has to make a choice.

611
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:50,868
Does he choose
safety and cowardice?

612
00:37:51,970 --> 00:37:55,031
Or does he opt for
courage and risk everything?

613
00:37:56,374 --> 00:37:58,002
I choose courage.

614
00:38:01,646 --> 00:38:03,478
What I'm trying to say
is... (CLEARS THROAT)

615
00:38:05,016 --> 00:38:08,418
The thing I've been wanting
to tell you all day long is...

616
00:38:11,656 --> 00:38:13,022
I love you.

617
00:38:14,392 --> 00:38:15,416
(CHUCKLES)

618
00:38:29,674 --> 00:38:33,076
(FRENCH MUSIC PLAYING ON STEREO)

619
00:38:37,448 --> 00:38:40,441
Impossible to pick the
perfect bottle, isn't it?

620
00:38:40,785 --> 00:38:43,584
Well, it all depends
on region and vintage.

621
00:38:43,988 --> 00:38:46,651
Of course, you have to
consider the wine pairing.

622
00:38:53,398 --> 00:38:57,335
- Ms. Kringle?
- No. Oh, no, my name's Isabella.

623
00:38:57,769 --> 00:39:01,228
Um, I'm sorry to bother you.
I don't usually talk to people.

624
00:39:01,506 --> 00:39:03,668
There's just
something about you.

625
00:39:03,942 --> 00:39:05,467
No, no, please, there's...

626
00:39:07,045 --> 00:39:08,877
There's no need to apologize.

627
00:39:09,214 --> 00:39:10,214
(STAMMERS)

628
00:39:11,683 --> 00:39:14,619
You remind me of
someone that I used to know.

629
00:39:15,386 --> 00:39:16,945
Long time ago.

630
00:39:23,261 --> 00:39:24,957
You struggle to regain me.

631
00:39:25,296 --> 00:39:28,698
When I'm lost, you
struggle to obtain me.

632
00:39:29,767 --> 00:39:31,201
What am I?

633
00:39:33,137 --> 00:39:34,230
Time.

634
00:39:37,342 --> 00:39:38,605
I'm Edward.

635
00:39:40,078 --> 00:39:41,546
Edward Nygma.

636
00:39:49,821 --> 00:39:52,586
Jim, how is she?

637
00:39:53,324 --> 00:39:54,324
Still in surgery.

638
00:39:54,525 --> 00:39:56,525
She seems like a tough
cookie. She'll be all right.

639
00:39:56,995 --> 00:39:58,395
What about Tetch?

640
00:39:58,630 --> 00:40:02,590
We got the whole department
canvassing the city. We'll find him.

641
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:05,400
Why didn't you come to me?

642
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:08,234
I couldn't.

643
00:40:10,375 --> 00:40:12,241
And I thought I
could save 'em both.

644
00:40:13,177 --> 00:40:15,078
You did what you
thought was right.

645
00:40:15,346 --> 00:40:16,575
Maybe.

646
00:40:20,385 --> 00:40:23,184
In the end, I did
exactly what he wanted.

647
00:40:25,323 --> 00:40:26,552
He won.

648
00:40:31,629 --> 00:40:32,688
We'll see.

649
00:40:33,197 --> 00:40:34,597
(SIGHS)

650
00:40:43,007 --> 00:40:45,499
(WOMAN CHATTERING ON PA)

651
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:51,682
Mario's a great doctor.
She'll pull through.

652
00:40:57,322 --> 00:40:59,655
- Lee, about what I said...
- Jim.

653
00:41:01,092 --> 00:41:02,321
Not now.

654
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,346
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

655
00:42:04,422 --> 00:42:05,422
English -SDH
